msgstr "**WORKFLOW:** Select un/una vRO workflow desde el/la list synced desde el/la seleccionado/seleccionada integration"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:524
msgid "**PARAMETER BODY (JSON):**"
msgstr "**PARAMETER BODY (JSON):**"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:532
msgid ""
"**ATTRIBUTES:** A JSON map of arbitrary values to write to the attributes"
" property of the target resource"
msgstr "**ATTRIBUTES:** A JSON map of arbitrary values to write to the attributes property of the target resource"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:536
msgid ""
"This is often useful for storing values from one phase of a Provisioning "
"Workflow for access in another phase. See the video demo below for a "
"complete example."
msgstr "Este/Esta es often useful para storing values desde one phase de un/una Provisioning Flujo de trabajo para access en another phase. See el/la video demo abajo para un/una complete example."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:538
msgid ""
"There are a number of ways that a JSON payload can be statically drafted "
"within a Write Attributes Task or called into the Task as a result from a"
" prior Task. Consider the following examples:"
msgstr "There are a number of ways that a JSON payload puede ser statically drafted within a Write Attributes Tarea or called into the Tarea as a result from a prior Tarea. Consider the following examples:"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:540
msgid ""
"To pass in a static JSON map with static values, use the format shown "
"below."
msgstr "To pass en un/una static JSON map con static values, use el/la format shown below."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:542
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"my_key1\": \"my_value1\",\n"
"  \"my_key2\": \"my_value2\"\n"
"}"
msgstr "{\\n  \\\"my_key1\\\": \\\"my_value1\\\",\\n  \\\"my_key2\\\": \\\"my_value2\\\"\\n}"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:549
msgid ""
"To pass in a static JSON map with dynamic values seeded from prior Task "
"results, ensure the RESULT TYPE value of one or more of the prior Tasks "
"in the Workflow phase is set to \"Single Value\" and refer to the values "
"within the JSON map as shown in the next example. Note that \"taskCode1\""
" and \"taskCode2\" refer to the CODE field value for the Task whose "
"output you wish to reference."
msgstr "To pass en un/una static JSON map con dynamic values seeded desde prior Tarea results, ensure el/la RESULT TYPE value de one o más de el/la prior Tareas en el/la Flujo de trabajo phase es establecido/establecida a \"Single Value\" y refer a el/la values dentro de el/la JSON map como shown en el/la siguiente example. Note ese/esa \"taskCode1\" y \"taskCode2\" refer a el/la CODE field value para el/la Tarea whose output you wish a reference."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:551
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"my_key1\": \"<%=results.taskCode1%>\",\n"
"  \"my_key2\": \"<%=results.taskCode2%>\"\n"
"}"
msgstr "{\\n  \\\"my_key1\\\": \\\"<%=results.taskCode1%>\\\",\\n  \\\"my_key2\\\": \\\"<%=results.taskCode2%>\\\"\\n}"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:558
msgid ""
"To pass in a dynamic JSON map returned from a prior Task, format your "
"Write Attributes Task as shown in the next example. Ensure that the "
"RESULT TYPE value for the Task returning a JSON map is set to \"JSON\". "
"Note that \"taskCode\" in the example refers to the CODE field value for "
"the Task being referenced. In order for the JSON map to be set correctly "
"and able to be referenced from future Tasks, you must set the "
"\"instances\" key and call the ``encodeAsJSON()`` Groovy method as shown "
"in the example."
msgstr "To pass en un/una dynamic JSON map returned desde un/una prior Tarea, format your Write Attributes Tarea como shown en el/la siguiente example. Ensure ese/esa el/la RESULT TYPE value para el/la Tarea returning un/una JSON map es establecido/establecida a \"JSON\". Note ese/esa \"taskCode\" en el/la example refers a el/la CODE field value para el/la Tarea being referenced. In order para el/la JSON map a be establecido/establecida correctly y able a be referenced desde future Tareas, you debe/n establecido/establecida el/la \"instances\" key y call el/la ``encodeAsJSON()`` Groovy method como shown en el/la example."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:560
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"instances\": <%=results.taskCode?.encodeAsJSON()%>\n"
"}"
msgstr "{\\n  \\\"instances\\\": <%=results.taskCode?.encodeAsJSON()%>\\n}"

